From b441da3256da6bb1e21a4177a9f177cc4cb70be4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Razman Zaidi <100824525+idiazraz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:03:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Snap layouts for the KrissOS Shell (kriss_snap_v1)

A small protocol for the shell: snap(identifier, x, y, w, h) tiles a
floating window into a zone given in twelfths of its screen's work area,
through the same floating_tiled state as cosmic-comp's own snapping, so
Windows+arrows and dragging out behave as for a snapped half. Halves and
quarters map onto the existing TiledCorners; other zones (thirds) use a
new TiledCorners::Zone. maximize_hover(identifier, hovered) tells the
shell when the pointer enters or leaves the maximize button of a
server-side title bar, so it can offer the layouts there.
